     < deg Φ_i, hence LEVEL-i-FREE.  Witness check at i = 2:
     n̂₂ = x^iπ^aΦ′^b with i < e₁ = 2, b < e₂ = 2, max degree 1 + 2 = 3 <
     4 = deg Φ₂; and dv₂(Φ′) = 4·(5/4) = 5 = u₂, reproducing the source's own
     "u₂ = dv₂(Φ′)" row.  So EVERY normalizer height is reading-independent.
                                                                    CONSISTENT
  4. lift_i(d;m): (C3-lift-coefficient-space) forces deg < deg Φ_i, so the
     lift contract dv_i(lift) = m is reading-independent.  This is the load-
     bearing one: r12's binding cannot silently move a lift height. CONSISTENT
  5. (C1-stage-uniformizer) dv_i(π_{i+1}) = 1: a typed assumption, not a
     computed value; at level 1 it is discharged by ℓ₁h + ℓ′₁e₁ = 1 on a
     level-1-free monomial.  Value-group check at i = 2: dv₂ = 4ν takes values
     in (1/2)ℤ (ν in (1/8)ℤ), so 1 is attainable.                   CONSISTENT
  6. (C1-stage-key-height): the sole consumer that DISTINGUISHES the readings,
     and the one R12-1 pins.                                        CONSISTENT
  7. (C3-common-height) dv_i(k̂_tΦ_i^{e_{i+1}t}) = (s+t)u_{i+1}: only
     e_{i+1}-multiples of Φ_i occur, so integral and terminal-correct.
                                                                    CONSISTENT
  8. (C5)/(C6) dv₁ on polynomials of degree < D′.                   CONSISTENT
  9. Grades: κ̄_i = u_{i+1}/e(µ_i); at i = 2, 21/4 ∈ (1/4)ℤ = Λ₂ with
     e(µ₂) = 4.  β_t = (f_{i+1}−t)κ̄_i matches the source verbatim
